# --- point-in-time script backups (2026-10-05) ---
# Scripts that modify the verification gate write a dated backup beside
# themselves before editing, e.g. scripts/pristine_gate.sh.prefix_2026-10-05.
# These are IGNORED rather than tracked, and that is a deliberate, verified
# choice: each was confirmed byte-identical (`cmp`) to the version git already
# holds in the immediately preceding commit, so the content is fully
# recoverable from history and tracking it would only duplicate it. The files
# are left on disk as working copies, not deleted.
# NOTE: this entry exists so `git status` is HONESTLY clean. It is not a licence
# to ignore anything inconvenient -- a1_v4.sh was left untracked for days and
# then filtered out of status output, which made a "tree clean" report false.
# Anything whose content is NOT already in git gets TRACKED, never ignored.
*.prefix_20[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]

# pristine_gate.sh PremiseAudit probes: mktemp --suffix=.lean -p . leaves these
# in the repo root. Gate artifacts, never source. Added 2026-10-06 after one
# showed up untracked during a full-closure gate sweep.
probe_audit_*.lean
